WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.135 --> 00:00:02.601
-My next guest is
a successful businesswoman,

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:04.070
a best-selling author,

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:06.272
and her new show
"Cooking with Paris"

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:08.274
is streaming now on Netflix.

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:12.044
Everyone, please welcome
Paris Hilton!

00:00:12.044 --> 00:00:13.979
♪ -Paaaris Hilton ♪

00:00:13.979 --> 00:00:16.182
♪ Serving up some news ♪

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:18.150
♪ You're probably thinking ♪

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:20.519
♪ I wonder how she cooks ♪

00:00:20.519 --> 00:00:22.154
♪ So pay attention ♪

00:00:22.154 --> 00:00:25.424
♪ Might learn something
todaaaay ♪

00:00:25.424 --> 00:00:26.892
-Thank you so much.

00:00:26.892 --> 00:00:29.061
Welcome back to our show.

00:00:29.061 --> 00:00:30.196
Thanks for coming on.

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:31.731
-It's great to be here.

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:33.199
-There's lots to talk about.

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:35.434
I know that you just --
you got engaged.

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:37.136
-Yes.
-Are you --

00:00:37.136 --> 00:00:38.238
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:39.739
Congratulations.

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:41.640
Are you in the planning stages
now?

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:43.109
-Yes, we are planning
everything.

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:44.777
It's very stressful.

00:00:44.777 --> 00:00:46.912
-It's a lot of stuff.
Have you picked out a dress?

00:00:46.912 --> 00:00:49.582
-Yes, that's basically
the only thing that I've done.

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:50.717
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:51.985
It's a lot of stuff, though.

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:55.255
-It's a lot. It's --
But I'm not a Bridezilla at all.

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:56.756
-No, I didn't think
you would be, though.

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:58.658
I think that you would have this
under control.

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:01.394
But here's the one thing I
thought was actually brilliant.

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:05.832
You're documenting your wedding
for a show, a series on Peacock.

00:01:05.832 --> 00:01:08.534
-Yes.
-Why add that extra pressure?

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:11.604
-I just feel like for
my documentary, "This Is Paris,"

00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:14.373
it ended in a way in which,
you know, it was an amazing --

00:01:14.373 --> 00:01:16.676
but I just feel like
I wanted my fans to see

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:20.380
that I found my Prince Charming
and my happy fairy-tale ending.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:22.148
-Yeah. Yeah, good, I'm glad.

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:23.850
[ Applause ]

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:27.186
Are you going to --
I know you -- You deejay.

00:01:27.186 --> 00:01:30.657
You're one of the most famous
deejays out there.

00:01:30.657 --> 00:01:33.526
Are you going to deejay at
your own wedding or get a band?

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:35.261
[ Laughter ]
-Oh.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:38.397
I'll definitely get a deejay
because it's too much.

00:01:38.397 --> 00:01:39.499
We'll have a band as well.

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:41.600
It's gonna be like
a three-day affair.

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:43.102
-Oh, really?
-We have a lot happening.

00:01:43.102 --> 00:01:44.704
-Three days? Big deal.

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:46.538
-Yes.
-So more than one dress?

00:01:46.538 --> 00:01:49.542
-Lots of dresses. Probably 10.
I love outfit changes.

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:51.343
-Yes. 10 outfits?

00:01:51.343 --> 00:01:53.313
And how about
your husband-to-be?

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:54.680
Will he have outfit changes?

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:56.983
-He's not as high maintenance
as I am.

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:58.284
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:00.686
-When you deejay, do you get
upset when people come up

00:02:00.686 --> 00:02:03.389
to the booth and make requests?

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:04.924
-It depends on the request.

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:06.926
If it's like a brutal song,
yeah, that's annoying.

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:09.228
But if they have a good idea,
why not?

00:02:09.228 --> 00:02:10.630
-Oh, really?
-Yeah.

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:12.198
-How's your mom and dad doing?

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:14.800
-They're doing amazing.
-Your mom's a hit, by the way.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.669
She's on --
She's not a housewife

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:17.904
but she's on "Real Housewives."

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:20.006
And every time she's a hit.

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:21.274
-She's so funny.

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:23.643
-Did you -- Did she ask you
before she went on?

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:25.043
Like, "Hey, do you mind
if I do this?"

00:02:25.043 --> 00:02:26.779
-We read about it on TMZ.

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:29.982
My sister and I were,
like, terrified because

00:02:29.982 --> 00:02:31.817
we didn't want her getting
involved in all the drama.

00:02:31.817 --> 00:02:33.386
But I'm very proud of her.

00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:35.187
She's just herself. She's funny.

00:02:35.187 --> 00:02:36.923
And people are loving it.

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:38.157
So I'm really proud of her.

00:02:38.157 --> 00:02:40.259
-There was one that I saw
where, I think,

00:02:40.259 --> 00:02:42.562
she didn't know what a Red Bull
was or something

00:02:42.562 --> 00:02:44.430
or she didn't know
it kept you awake.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.765
And she ended up drinking it
and staying up all night.

00:02:46.765 --> 00:02:47.967
She couldn't go to sleep.

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:49.769
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:52.805
-How is "This Is Paris" going,
your podcast?

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:54.507
-It's so much fun. I love --

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:56.708
You know, I've been interviewed
like a billion times,

00:02:56.708 --> 00:02:58.311
so to be the one doing it

00:02:58.311 --> 00:03:00.479
and asking all the questions
is super fun.

00:03:00.479 --> 00:03:03.282
-I find the show interesting
because you are so interesting.

00:03:03.282 --> 00:03:04.684
You have so many things
going on.

00:03:04.684 --> 00:03:06.485
When you ask a question
and someone will get --

00:03:06.485 --> 00:03:09.255
some story will get brought up,
and you're like "Oh, yeah,"

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:10.589
and then you'll tell this story
like --

00:03:10.589 --> 00:03:12.959
I didn't know how into NFTs
you were.

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:14.393
Do you guys know what that is?

00:03:14.393 --> 00:03:15.861
-No.
-Yeah.

00:03:15.861 --> 00:03:17.163
Like 12 people know what it is.

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:18.497
[ Laughter ]
I barely know.

00:03:18.497 --> 00:03:20.633
Can you explain what an NFT is?

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:23.869
-It's a nonfungible token.
-Nonfungible.

00:03:23.869 --> 00:03:24.971
-Yes.
-Okay.

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:26.805
-Which is basically
a digital contract

00:03:26.805 --> 00:03:28.274
that's on the blockchain.

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:32.478
So you can basically have --
sell anything from art to music

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:36.516
to experiences,
physical objects.

00:03:36.516 --> 00:03:39.919
-I'm not going to jump into
the NFT world, but I would --

00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:42.087
I know Beeple is an artist

00:03:42.087 --> 00:03:44.524
that's awesome.
-Yeah, so awesome.

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:49.361
-And he had maybe like 300
pictures in one digital picture.

00:03:49.361 --> 00:03:50.696
I thought that was interesting.

00:03:50.696 --> 00:03:52.799
And I go, "Well, I could never
do that, what he did."

00:03:52.799 --> 00:03:55.068
-Yeah.
You could try something maybe.

00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:57.203
Like sell one of your jokes
or something.

00:03:57.203 --> 00:03:58.604
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.604 --> 00:04:00.373
-I couldn't even do that
to my audience tonight.

00:04:00.373 --> 00:04:02.108
Are you kidding me?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.108 --> 00:04:05.611
I doubt I would make money off
the NFTs.

00:04:05.611 --> 00:04:09.182
I want to talk about
"Cooking with Paris" because --

00:04:09.182 --> 00:04:11.117
you know,
with all these projects,

00:04:11.117 --> 00:04:12.951
I get to know you more and more.

00:04:12.951 --> 00:04:15.855
"This Is Paris,"
when you made that, I go, "Wow."

00:04:15.855 --> 00:04:18.157
That was so interesting to see
that side of you,

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:20.392
and it just was very --
I loved it.

00:04:20.392 --> 00:04:22.361
And this, the one I saw,

00:04:22.361 --> 00:04:24.296
the episode is
you and Kim Kardashian.

00:04:24.296 --> 00:04:26.265
How long have you known
each other, you and Kim?

00:04:26.265 --> 00:04:28.134
-Since we were little girls,
our whole life.

00:04:28.134 --> 00:04:31.036
-Yeah. And how many times
have you cooked together?

00:04:31.036 --> 00:04:33.806
-Back in the day when we would
go out at night, like,

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:36.975
we'd come home late, and, like,
make grilled cheeses or --

00:04:36.975 --> 00:04:38.911
-Really? What's your secret
to grilled cheese?

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:41.981
-Brioche bread, cheddar cheese,
lots of butter.

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:43.249
-Mmm.

00:04:43.249 --> 00:04:47.719
I go Wonder Bread, American
Kraft singles, and yeah.

00:04:47.719 --> 00:04:49.455
I could also do --
Yeah, lots of butter, yeah.

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:51.324
And make sure the pan is hot.
-Yes.

00:04:51.324 --> 00:04:52.992
-Yeah, I do love
a grilled cheese. Gosh.

00:04:52.992 --> 00:04:55.127
I want to show everyone a clip
from the show.

00:04:55.127 --> 00:04:57.596
Here are Paris Hilton
and Kim Kardashian

00:04:57.596 --> 00:04:59.298
on "Cooking with Paris."

00:04:59.298 --> 00:05:00.366
Take a look at this.

00:05:00.366 --> 00:05:01.800
-This is how it used to be.

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:04.102
Paris would have the ideas,
and I'd come in and be like,

00:05:04.102 --> 00:05:05.571
"This is never going to
work out.

00:05:05.571 --> 00:05:07.439
Like, this is not practical."

00:05:07.439 --> 00:05:08.774
-You're the organized one.

00:05:08.774 --> 00:05:11.877
I'm like the most disorganized
person in the world.

00:05:11.877 --> 00:05:13.513
♪♪

00:05:13.513 --> 00:05:14.780
This might work.

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:16.248
-We got --
[ Chuckles ]

00:05:16.248 --> 00:05:18.017
-Oh, that's cute.

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:19.285
Killing it.

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:22.855
If this was cookies,
it would work, right?

00:05:22.855 --> 00:05:25.524
-I'm going to need to,
like, touch up my makeup.

00:05:25.524 --> 00:05:27.459
I'm literally crying.

00:05:27.459 --> 00:05:32.631
The fact that you thought
these marshmallows could work.

00:05:32.631 --> 00:05:34.166
Oh, my God. Oh, my God.

00:05:34.166 --> 00:05:36.035
Wait, do I have blue
all over my face?

00:05:36.035 --> 00:05:38.237
-[ Laughs ]
Paris Hilton, everybody.

00:05:38.237 --> 00:05:41.741
"Cooking with Paris"
is streaming now on Netflix.

